IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dog-act-domain`

-- =============================================================================
-- Dog Act 1976 (Western Australia) -- Part IX, "Local laws" (ss 48-52)
--
-- Isomorphic encoding of ss 48, 49, 49A, 49B, 50, 51 and 52, as at the
-- compilation dated 28 Nov 2024 [version 08-b0-00], re-verified current
-- 2026-09-09. Source lines 1668-1720 of mrdoc_47983.txt
-- (canon/subjects/western-australia/dog-act-1976/registers/source-bundle).
--
-- Unlike Part VI Division 1/2 (dog-act-1976.l4), this Part is not about
-- dog-owner offences: it is the machinery by which the Governor and local
-- governments MAKE, AMEND and REVOKE regulations and local laws under this
-- Act. Accordingly this module reuses only `LiableParty` from
-- dog-act-domain.l4 (at s 51(c), which re-creates the s 3 "person liable for
-- the control of the dog" test verbatim in a local-law-making-power
-- context); `DogProfile`, `AttackFacts` and `Penalty` have no natural role
-- here and are deliberately not used.
--
-- SCOPED OUT (cited at their site with @ref, never expanded): Local
-- Government Act 1995 (WA) Subdivision 2 of Division 2 of Part 3 (s 49(b))
-- and s 3.17 (s 49B(5)); Part III Division 1 ss 14-20 of this Act (dog
-- registration, s 51(a)); s 29 and s 33G of this Act (seizure/destruction
-- powers, ss 51(f)-(g)).
--
-- Two ambiguities were found, both undefined evaluative standards delegated
-- to fact-supply following this corpus's existing precedent
-- (F-REPEATEDLY-TENDENCY / F-33H-SATISFACTION-STANDARD in dog-act-1976.l4):
-- F-NO-REASONABLE-RELATIONSHIP (s 49B(2)) and F-UNDULY-OPPRESSIVE-STANDARD
-- (s 52(1)). See the sites below and the returned ambiguities register.
--
-- Several subsections are pure administrative/discretionary machinery with
-- no fact a downstream rule would ever need to test (the Governor's/local
-- government's/Minister's own decision to exercise a law-making power, and
-- the saving clauses protecting things already done). These are recorded as
-- plain "--" comments at their site rather than force-fit into meaningless
-- always-TRUE predicates.
-- =============================================================================

§ `Local law purposes -- shared type (used by ss 48(2), 49(c) and 51)`

-- s 48(2) ties the permissible subject matter of a s 48 regulation to "any
-- matter in respect of which local laws may be made under this Act" -- i.e.
-- exactly the purposes s 51 (below) permits. s 49(c) makes the same tie
-- explicitly ("for the purposes permitted by section 51"). Rather than
-- declare the enum where s 51 sits in the Act's own order and forward-
-- reference it from ss 48/49, it is hoisted here once, exactly as this
-- corpus's main file hoists its "Shared penalty presets" ahead of the Part
-- they serve. (b) and (h) are omitted below because s 51 itself marks them
-- "[deleted]".
DECLARE `S51 Purpose` IS ONE OF
    `registration of dogs (s 51(a))`
    `dog excreta on streets or public places without consent (s 51(c))`
    `fenced premises requirement (s 51(d))`
    `dog management facilities and services (s 51(e))`
    `detention, maintenance, care, release or disposal of seized dogs (s 51(f))`
    `destruction of dogs pursuant to powers conferred (s 51(g))`
    `licensing, regulating, construction, use and inspection of approved kennel establishments (s 51(i))`

§ `Part IX -- Local laws`
§§ `48. Regulations to operate as local laws`

-- s 48(1): the Governor's own discretionary power to make s 48 regulations
-- for a district. A bare grant of legislative power, not a fact this
-- encoding tests.

-- s 48(2): see the `S51 Purpose` type above -- a s 48 regulation may deal
-- with any matter a local law may be made about under s 51.

DECLARE `S48 Regulation` HAS
    `regulation only repeals or amends other regulations made under this section`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains a statement that it applies as if it were a local law`                IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 48(3)
GIVEN reg IS A `S48 Regulation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 48(3) content requirement is satisfied` reg MEANS
        reg's `regulation only repeals or amends other regulations made under this section`
    OR  reg's `contains a statement that it applies as if it were a local law`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 48(4)
GIVEN `the regulation relates to a place where the local government may perform functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the local government must administer the s 48 regulation as if it were a local law` `the regulation relates to a place where the local government may perform functions` MEANS
    `the regulation relates to a place where the local government may perform functions`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 48(5)
GIVEN `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a reference to an offence against a local law includes an offence against a s 48 regulation` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    NOT `a contrary intention appears`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 48(6)
GIVEN `inconsistency exists between a s 48 regulation and a local law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 48 regulation prevails over the local law under s 48(6)` `inconsistency exists between a s 48 regulation and a local law` MEANS
    `inconsistency exists between a s 48 regulation and a local law`

§§ `49. Local laws`

DECLARE `S49 LocalLawFacts` HAS
    `for the local government's district, or an area regarded (for the purposes of this Act) as being within that district` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in accordance with Subdivision 2 of Division 2 of Part 3 of the Local Government Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Local Government Act 1995 (WA) Part 3 Div 2 Subdiv 2 -- scoped out, fact-supplied (external Act)
    purpose IS A `S51 Purpose`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 49
GIVEN f IS A `S49 LocalLawFacts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a local government may make a s 49 local law` f MEANS
        f's `for the local government's district, or an area regarded (for the purposes of this Act) as being within that district`
    AND f's `made in accordance with Subdivision 2 of Division 2 of Part 3 of the Local Government Act 1995`
    -- s 49(c) is satisfied by construction: `purpose` is typed as `S51 Purpose`,
    -- i.e. a purpose s 51 (below) permits.

§§ `49A. Model local laws`

-- s 49A(1): the Governor's own discretionary power to prepare and publish
-- model local laws for adoption by reference. Not a fact this encoding tests.

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 49A(2)
GIVEN `the model local law provision has been adopted by a local law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a model local law provision has effect` `the model local law provision has been adopted by a local law` MEANS
    `the model local law provision has been adopted by a local law`

-- s 49A(3): the Governor's own discretionary power to amend a published
-- model local law by Gazette notice. Not a fact this encoding tests.

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 49A(4)
GIVEN `the local law's adoption of the model local law occurred before the amendment was made` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a further local law has since adopted the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the amendment to a model local law applies to the local law` `the local law's adoption of the model local law occurred before the amendment was made` `a further local law has since adopted the amendment` MEANS
        (NOT `the local law's adoption of the model local law occurred before the amendment was made`)
    OR  `a further local law has since adopted the amendment`

§§ `49B. Governor may amend or repeal local laws`

-- s 49B(1): the Governor's own discretionary power to make a local law
-- amending the text of, or repealing, a local law. Not a fact this
-- encoding tests -- s 49B(2) below encodes the one real limit on it.

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 49B(2)
-- AMBIGUITY (F-NO-REASONABLE-RELATIONSHIP): "a provision that bears no
-- reasonable relationship to the local law as in force before the
-- amendment" (s 49B(2)) states no test of its own. Delegated to
-- fact-supply, following this corpus's existing precedent for undefined
-- evaluative standards (F-33H-SATISFACTION-STANDARD, F-REPEATEDLY-TENDENCY
-- in dog-act-1976.l4).
GIVEN `the s 49B(1) amendment introduces a provision that bears no reasonable relationship to the local law as it stood before the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a s 49B(1) amendment is within the Governor's power` `the s 49B(1) amendment introduces a provision that bears no reasonable relationship to the local law as it stood before the amendment` MEANS
    NOT `the s 49B(1) amendment introduces a provision that bears no reasonable relationship to the local law as it stood before the amendment`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 49B(3)
GIVEN `the Minister has given the local government written notice of the s 49B local law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 49B(3) notice duty is discharged` `the Minister has given the local government written notice of the s 49B local law` MEANS
    `the Minister has given the local government written notice of the s 49B local law`
    -- No numeric deadline is stated for this duty (contrast s 52(2) below,
    -- which does state one and so is encoded as a PARTY/MUST/WITHIN rule).

-- s 49B(4): a local law made under s 49B is deemed, for all purposes, to be
-- a local law made by the local government whose local law was amended or
-- repealed. A pure attribution/deeming rule with no branching content, and
-- no downstream rule in this chunk reads "who made it" -- not encoded.

-- s 49B(5): s 3.17 of the Local Government Act 1995 (WA) does not apply to
-- local laws made under this section. A disapplication of an external
-- provision this encoding does not otherwise reach; not a computed fact.

§§ `50. General provisions relating to regulations and local laws`

-- s 50(1)(a): a regulation/local law may vary its scope of application by
-- case, time and place (including areas treated as within the district).
-- Drafting latitude, not itself a testable fact.

-- s 50(1)(b): a regulation/local law may require conformity with a
-- specified standard, or approval by/to the satisfaction of a specified
-- person or body, and may delegate discretionary authority to a specified
-- body. Drafting latitude, not itself a testable fact.

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 50(1)(c)
GIVEN `the case is a specified case, or falls within a specified class of case, for exemption` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `any specified conditions for the exemption are satisfied, or the exemption is unconditional` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person or thing is exempted under a s 50(1)(c) provision` `the case is a specified case, or falls within a specified class of case, for exemption` `any specified conditions for the exemption are satisfied, or the exemption is unconditional` MEANS
        `the case is a specified case, or falls within a specified class of case, for exemption`
    AND `any specified conditions for the exemption are satisfied, or the exemption is unconditional`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 50(2)
GIVEN `the specified penalty amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a s 48 regulation or local law's penalty provision is within the s 50(2) cap` `the specified penalty amount` MEANS
    `the specified penalty amount` AT MOST 5_000
    -- s 50(2) also empowers prescribing fees/charges, the persons liable and
    -- the method of recovery -- administrative machinery, not a computed fact.

-- s 50(3): "specified" means specified in the regulation or local law
-- itself, unless the context requires otherwise -- an ordinary drafting-
-- convention interpretation clause, not itself a testable fact.

§§ `51. Local law making powers`

-- The `S51 Purpose` enum is declared above (hoisted for ss 48(2)/49(c)).
-- (b) and (h) are marked "[deleted]" in the source and so have no
-- constructor.

-- s 51(a): providing for the registration of dogs.
    -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) Part III Division 1, ss 14-20 (dog registration) -- outside this chunk's line range, scoped out

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 51(c)
GIVEN party IS A LiableParty,
      `the dog excreted on a street, public place, or land, without the consent of the occupier, within an area a s 51(c) local law specifies` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the excreta was removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`conduct within the scope of a s 51(c) local law -- permitting a dog to excrete without removal` party `the dog excreted on a street, public place, or land, without the consent of the occupier, within an area a s 51(c) local law specifies` `the excreta was removed` MEANS
        `the party is a person liable for the control of the dog` party
    AND `the dog excreted on a street, public place, or land, without the consent of the occupier, within an area a s 51(c) local law specifies`
    AND NOT `the excreta was removed`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 51(d)
GIVEN `a portion of the premises where the dog is kept is fenced in a manner capable of confining the dog` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the premises comply with a s 51(d) local law's fencing requirement` `a portion of the premises where the dog is kept is fenced in a manner capable of confining the dog` MEANS
    `a portion of the premises where the dog is kept is fenced in a manner capable of confining the dog`

-- s 51(e): providing for the establishment and maintenance of dog
-- management facilities and other services/facilities. Administrative
-- machinery, not itself a testable fact.

-- s 51(f): providing for the detention, maintenance, care, release or
-- disposal of seized dogs.
    -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 29 -- power to seize/detain generally, outside this chunk, scoped out

-- s 51(g): as to the destruction of dogs pursuant to the powers
-- "hereinbefore conferred".
    -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 33G -- seizure and destruction (dangerous dogs), outside this chunk, scoped out

-- s 51(i): providing for the licensing, regulating, construction, use and
-- inspection of approved kennel establishments. Administrative machinery,
-- with no criterion stated in this Part for what makes a kennel
-- establishment "approved" -- not itself a testable fact here.

§§ `52. Revocation of local laws`

DECLARE `S52 Revocation Grounds` HAS
    `relates to a matter affecting dogs or the keeping of dogs`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the Governor's opinion, the local law (or the manner of its administration) is unduly oppressive`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the Governor's opinion, the local law (or the manner of its administration) is repugnant to the provisions of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the Governor's opinion, the local law (or the manner of its administration) is inconsistent with the provisions of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 52(1)
-- AMBIGUITY (F-UNDULY-OPPRESSIVE-STANDARD): "unduly oppressive, repugnant to
-- or inconsistent with the provisions of this Act" (s 52(1)) states no test
-- of its own. Delegated to the Governor's own opinion, per s 52(1)'s own
-- "in the opinion of the Governor" language -- the same treatment this
-- corpus already gives F-REPEATEDLY-TENDENCY and F-33H-SATISFACTION-STANDARD
-- in dog-act-1976.l4. The two possible subjects of that opinion -- "that
-- local law" itself, or "the manner in which that local law is
-- administered" -- are folded into one generic ground-check field per
-- limb below, since the grounds test is identical either way.
GIVEN g IS A `S52 Revocation Grounds`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Governor may revoke a local law (or part of it) under s 52(1)` g MEANS
        g's `relates to a matter affecting dogs or the keeping of dogs`
    AND (   g's `in the Governor's opinion, the local law (or the manner of its administration) is unduly oppressive`
         OR g's `in the Governor's opinion, the local law (or the manner of its administration) is repugnant to the provisions of this Act`
         OR g's `in the Governor's opinion, the local law (or the manner of its administration) is inconsistent with the provisions of this Act`)

-- s 52(1) saving clause: a s 52(1) revocation does not affect the validity,
-- or cure the invalidity, of anything done (or any omission) in the
-- meantime. Not a computed fact -- there is no fact this encoding derives
-- from a saving clause, per the same treatment given s 33D(3) in
-- dog-act-1976.l4.

-- The Act does not distinguish the Legislative Assembly from the
-- Legislative Council for this duty -- "each House" gets the identical
-- 6/14-sitting-day treatment -- so both are modelled as one generic
-- `House of Parliament` actor, the same simplification this corpus already
-- makes collapsing s 33K(2)/(3) into one DogActAction constructor.
DECLARE `S52 Party` IS ONE OF
    Minister
    `House of Parliament`

DECLARE `S52 Action` IS ONE OF
    `lay a copy of the s 52 revocation notice before a House of Parliament`
    `pass a disallowance resolution against the s 52 revocation notice, notice of the resolution having been given`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 52(2)
`s 52(2) duty -- laying the revocation notice before Parliament` MEANS
    PARTY Minister
    MUST  `lay a copy of the s 52 revocation notice before a House of Parliament`
    WITHIN 6
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY Minister
          BECAUSE "a copy of the s 52 revocation notice was not laid before the House within 6 sitting days, as s 52(2) requires"

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 52(2)
`s 52(2) -- a House's option to disallow the notice` MEANS
    PARTY `House of Parliament`
    MAY   `pass a disallowance resolution against the s 52 revocation notice, notice of the resolution having been given`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  FULFILLED

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 52(2)
GIVEN `a disallowance resolution against the notice was passed, notice of the resolution having been given` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `sitting days since the copy was laid before that House` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 52(1) notice ceases to have effect under s 52(2)` `a disallowance resolution against the notice was passed, notice of the resolution having been given` `sitting days since the copy was laid before that House` MEANS
        `a disallowance resolution against the notice was passed, notice of the resolution having been given`
    AND `sitting days since the copy was laid before that House` AT MOST 14

-- s 52(2) saving clause: the disallowance of the notice does not affect or
-- invalidate anything done in good faith before the resolution passed. Not
-- a computed fact, per the same treatment as the s 52(1) saving clause
-- above.

-- =============================================================================
-- Illustrations
-- =============================================================================

§ `Illustrations`

`a compliant repeal-only s 48 regulation` MEANS `S48 Regulation` WITH
    `regulation only repeals or amends other regulations made under this section` IS TRUE
    , `contains a statement that it applies as if it were a local law` IS FALSE

`a non-compliant new-matter s 48 regulation` MEANS `S48 Regulation` WITH
    `regulation only repeals or amends other regulations made under this section` IS FALSE
    , `contains a statement that it applies as if it were a local law` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the s 48(3) content requirement is satisfied` `a compliant repeal-only s 48 regulation`
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 48(3) content requirement is satisfied` `a non-compliant new-matter s 48 regulation`)

#ASSERT `the local government must administer the s 48 regulation as if it were a local law` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the local government must administer the s 48 regulation as if it were a local law` FALSE)

#ASSERT `a reference to an offence against a local law includes an offence against a s 48 regulation` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a reference to an offence against a local law includes an offence against a s 48 regulation` TRUE)

#ASSERT `the s 48 regulation prevails over the local law under s 48(6)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 48 regulation prevails over the local law under s 48(6)` FALSE)

`a compliant district local law, for an s 51(c) purpose` MEANS `S49 LocalLawFacts` WITH
    `for the local government's district, or an area regarded (for the purposes of this Act) as being within that district` IS TRUE
    , `made in accordance with Subdivision 2 of Division 2 of Part 3 of the Local Government Act 1995` IS TRUE
    , purpose IS `dog excreta on streets or public places without consent (s 51(c))`

`a local law for an area outside the district, made without following the LGA 1995 procedure` MEANS `S49 LocalLawFacts` WITH
    `for the local government's district, or an area regarded (for the purposes of this Act) as being within that district` IS FALSE
    , `made in accordance with Subdivision 2 of Division 2 of Part 3 of the Local Government Act 1995` IS FALSE
    , purpose IS `dog excreta on streets or public places without consent (s 51(c))`

`a local law for the district, but not made following the LGA 1995 procedure` MEANS `S49 LocalLawFacts` WITH
    `for the local government's district, or an area regarded (for the purposes of this Act) as being within that district` IS TRUE
    , `made in accordance with Subdivision 2 of Division 2 of Part 3 of the Local Government Act 1995` IS FALSE
    , purpose IS `dog excreta on streets or public places without consent (s 51(c))`

#ASSERT `a local government may make a s 49 local law` `a compliant district local law, for an s 51(c) purpose`
#ASSERT NOT (`a local government may make a s 49 local law` `a local law for an area outside the district, made without following the LGA 1995 procedure`)
-- distinguishes AND from OR: district requirement alone (s 49(a)) is not enough without the s 49(b) LGA 1995 procedure requirement
#ASSERT NOT (`a local government may make a s 49 local law` `a local law for the district, but not made following the LGA 1995 procedure`)

#ASSERT `a model local law provision has effect` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a model local law provision has effect` FALSE)

-- adopted after the amendment (not "before") -- the amendment simply applies
#ASSERT `the amendment to a model local law applies to the local law` FALSE FALSE
-- adopted before the amendment, and no further local law has adopted it since -- amendment does not apply
#ASSERT NOT (`the amendment to a model local law applies to the local law` TRUE FALSE)
-- adopted before the amendment, but a further local law has since adopted the amendment -- amendment applies
#ASSERT `the amendment to a model local law applies to the local law` TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `a s 49B(1) amendment is within the Governor's power` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a s 49B(1) amendment is within the Governor's power` TRUE)

#ASSERT `the s 49B(3) notice duty is discharged` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 49B(3) notice duty is discharged` FALSE)

#ASSERT `a person or thing is exempted under a s 50(1)(c) provision` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a person or thing is exempted under a s 50(1)(c) provision` TRUE FALSE)

#ASSERT `a s 48 regulation or local law's penalty provision is within the s 50(2) cap` 5_000
#ASSERT NOT (`a s 48 regulation or local law's penalty provision is within the s 50(2) cap` 5_001)

`the excreta-case dog owner` MEANS LiableParty WITH
    `is the registered owner of the dog` IS TRUE
    , `is the owner of the dog` IS TRUE
    , `is the occupier of premises where the dog is ordinarily kept or ordinarily permitted to live` IS TRUE
    , `has the dog in possession or under control` IS TRUE
    , `is a veterinarian, or acting on a veterinarian's behalf, in professional practice` IS FALSE
    , `is a police officer or other person acting under statutory duty or administering this Act` IS FALSE

`the excreta-case police officer` MEANS LiableParty WITH
    `is the registered owner of the dog` IS FALSE
    , `is the owner of the dog` IS FALSE
    , `is the occupier of premises where the dog is ordinarily kept or ordinarily permitted to live` IS FALSE
    , `has the dog in possession or under control` IS TRUE
    , `is a veterinarian, or acting on a veterinarian's behalf, in professional practice` IS FALSE
    , `is a police officer or other person acting under statutory duty or administering this Act` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `conduct within the scope of a s 51(c) local law -- permitting a dog to excrete without removal` `the excreta-case dog owner` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`conduct within the scope of a s 51(c) local law -- permitting a dog to excrete without removal` `the excreta-case dog owner` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`conduct within the scope of a s 51(c) local law -- permitting a dog to excrete without removal` `the excreta-case police officer` TRUE FALSE)

#ASSERT `the premises comply with a s 51(d) local law's fencing requirement` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the premises comply with a s 51(d) local law's fencing requirement` FALSE)

`grounds -- oppressive local law affecting dogs` MEANS `S52 Revocation Grounds` WITH
    `relates to a matter affecting dogs or the keeping of dogs` IS TRUE
    , `in the Governor's opinion, the local law (or the manner of its administration) is unduly oppressive` IS TRUE
    , `in the Governor's opinion, the local law (or the manner of its administration) is repugnant to the provisions of this Act` IS FALSE
    , `in the Governor's opinion, the local law (or the manner of its administration) is inconsistent with the provisions of this Act` IS FALSE

`grounds -- unobjectionable local law unrelated to dogs` MEANS `S52 Revocation Grounds` WITH
    `relates to a matter affecting dogs or the keeping of dogs` IS FALSE
    , `in the Governor's opinion, the local law (or the manner of its administration) is unduly oppressive` IS TRUE
    , `in the Governor's opinion, the local law (or the manner of its administration) is repugnant to the provisions of this Act` IS FALSE
    , `in the Governor's opinion, the local law (or the manner of its administration) is inconsistent with the provisions of this Act` IS FALSE

`grounds -- dog-related local law with no ground made out` MEANS `S52 Revocation Grounds` WITH
    `relates to a matter affecting dogs or the keeping of dogs` IS TRUE
    , `in the Governor's opinion, the local law (or the manner of its administration) is unduly oppressive` IS FALSE
    , `in the Governor's opinion, the local law (or the manner of its administration) is repugnant to the provisions of this Act` IS FALSE
    , `in the Governor's opinion, the local law (or the manner of its administration) is inconsistent with the provisions of this Act` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the Governor may revoke a local law (or part of it) under s 52(1)` `grounds -- oppressive local law affecting dogs`
#ASSERT NOT (`the Governor may revoke a local law (or part of it) under s 52(1)` `grounds -- unobjectionable local law unrelated to dogs`)
-- distinguishes AND from OR: relating to dogs is not itself sufficient -- at least one of the
-- three s 52(1) grounds (oppressive / repugnant / inconsistent) must also be made out
#ASSERT NOT (`the Governor may revoke a local law (or part of it) under s 52(1)` `grounds -- dog-related local law with no ground made out`)

#ASSERT `the s 52(1) notice ceases to have effect under s 52(2)` TRUE 10
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 52(1) notice ceases to have effect under s 52(2)` TRUE 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 52(1) notice ceases to have effect under s 52(2)` FALSE 10)

#TRACE `s 52(2) duty -- laying the revocation notice before Parliament` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Minister DOES `lay a copy of the s 52 revocation notice before a House of Parliament` AT 5
-- Result: FULFILLED (laid within the 6-sitting-day window)

#TRACE `s 52(2) duty -- laying the revocation notice before Parliament` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 7)
-- Result: DEONTIC BREACHED -- not laid before the House within 6 sitting days

#TRACE `s 52(2) -- a House's option to disallow the notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `House of Parliament` DOES `pass a disallowance resolution against the s 52 revocation notice, notice of the resolution having been given` AT 10
-- Result: FULFILLED (disallowance resolution passed within the 14-sitting-day window)
